{"event_type":"review","id":"0c05352419abbb46d265c1e8859c18b33f4a3ae2bf8daf4becf39c994ac1adb1","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T21:31:35Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d262e1347276f64852ab3c6baabf4971f3171b65398693190cf42a3f1621a365","sha256":"d262e1347276f64852ab3c6baabf4971f3171b65398693190cf42a3f1621a365"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c92e12ddfd17efea440d0e9f25c13bb5a63c820fad04fa964d4d595fdaf6c950","sha256":"c92e12ddfd17efea440d0e9f25c13bb5a63c820fad04fa964d4d595fdaf6c950"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/de60875720f51651a820f7b3a48513e0ed7af4011500e700c623ed7d30386cd3","sha256":"de60875720f51651a820f7b3a48513e0ed7af4011500e700c623ed7d30386cd3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3731382f09c84087070c7c3fd722f28234c56cf40f759a728f57a01827b174af","sha256":"3731382f09c84087070c7c3fd722f28234c56cf40f759a728f57a01827b174af"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c1b6d3a797ee2f6c95295837da1e211c78ccc3eb54b038a2106b694afa80a772","sha256":"c1b6d3a797ee2f6c95295837da1e211c78ccc3eb54b038a2106b694afa80a772"}],"attempt_id":"7d81eb259b9441139665294bda42cbb371d6fdab3e3710e76b0a27ffff7ae536:0:1","base":"f3125a6752fc5be3c52aca291c4cd76872bee01c","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"260297c7810eb197885396af3dc3ec0a5651abbe","body":"**Track every request bound to an item when matching an explicit predecessor.**\n\nTwo requests can bind the same item. `admit()` joins, reuses, or observes an existing equivalent item for a later non-repeat request (`src/policy/crq/reviewAdmission.ts:279-292`), then writes that request's binding to the same item ID (`:340`). `entriesFor` builds `byItem` with first-wins semantics (`src/policy/crq/reviewHistory.ts:235`), so the item keeps only the first request ID. When the predecessor is a later request, the explicit check at `:244` is false, and the linked row carries the earlier request ID (`:261`). The explicit fallback at `:451` then skips the item because it is already linked. The observation loop at `:495` skips the row because its request ID does not match the predecessor. When the server cannot establish ancestry, the predecessor is projected as `possible` with `repeat: false`, even when the client observation reports `ancestor: true`.\n\nStore every request ID bound to each item. Match the predecessor against that set. When it matches, set the linked row's `requestId` to the predecessor, so the observation at `:495` and the repeat check at `:524` apply.","id":"4ee90becdefd6714fe193a6cedf7721ed0a80f9ff3d51965722c9840d43b33e1","intervals":[[235,235]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reviewHistory.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Track every request bound to an item when matching an explicit predecessor."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"260297c7810eb197885396af3dc3ec0a5651abbe","body":"**Keep known commit distance in the delta when the tree is missing.**\n\nWhen `headline.delta` is null, the `else if` branch at `src/policy/crq/reviewHistory.ts:556` writes `commits_ahead: null`, even when `headline.commitsAhead` is known. The predecessor object reports the same distance (`src/policy/crq/reviewHistory.ts:595`), so the response reports two commits in one place and an unknown distance in another. The cue then states \"commit distance unknown (shallow or missing history)\" for a repository with known ancestry, which is inaccurate. Use the known value in the fallback delta:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     delta = withFields(\n       delta ??\n         new JsonObject([\n           ['method', 'tree'],\n           ['files', null],\n           ['insertions', null],\n           ['deletions', null],\n           ['binary_files', null],\n           ['partial', true],\n         ]),\n       [\n-        ['commits_ahead', null],\n+        [\n+          'commits_ahead',\n+          headline.commitsAhead === null ? null : JsonNumber.int(headline.commitsAhead),\n+        ],\n         ['ancestry', headline.ancestry],\n       ],\n     );\n```\n\n</details>\n\nApply the same change to the Python oracle at `apps/crq-python/review_history.py:309`, which has the same `\"commits_ahead\": None` branch. Change both implementations together to keep parity.","id":"1fc2a56f48ed0d993ec20836eac08de15ee52e2e0e299bf8ad2e933d2e19b1d4","intervals":[[539,539]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reviewHistory.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep known commit distance in the delta when the tree is missing."}],"head":"36ae10e37ee4dfb1930593b6a5365a7ee1546782","head_tree":"bda143e5c3801b7c35ed31c000807c5f716cf6f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"7225895e16de03193d1107763f8800ac42ad06f1","intervals":[[1,600]],"path":"src/policy/crq/backfillAccounting.ts"},{"blob":"8d07331ff6ba3d21cb5de6cc9bd9947de58ea35a","intervals":[[1,1308]],"path":"src/policy/crq/backfillInventory.ts"},{"blob":"4563b6265aa2d94c852e02e2fb41414bc00969ce","intervals":[[1,517]],"path":"src/policy/crq/backfillJobs.ts"},{"blob":"b4c94b5e8eae3a9112dd33c33e4187e3b056e676","intervals":[[1,572]],"path":"src/policy/crq/backfillReport.ts"},{"blob":"ecfff63e1d421ab9d556b29573a4a2a2c9385a5e","intervals":[[1,679]],"path":"src/policy/crq/jsonValue.ts"},{"blob":"675eb2c29d0aa6368a096c8bf208a708d7790669","intervals":[[1,547]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reconcileCheckpoint.ts"},{"blob":"25958c3a8b3ea9769371b453ba4fde552ea55f6b","intervals":[[1,726]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reconcileInventory.ts"},{"blob":"260297c7810eb197885396af3dc3ec0a5651abbe","intervals":[[1,695]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reviewHistory.ts"}],"job_id":"7d81eb259b9441139665294bda42cbb371d6fdab3e3710e76b0a27ffff7ae536:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason"